{
  "abstract": "We prove that every synchronous bounded-width layered digit support of size $O(n^{2-\\delta})$, for any fixed $\\delta>0$, has no-three-in-line capacity $O(n^{1-\\varepsilon})$. The programs may be nondeterministic, their transitions may depend on position and depth, and selection from the accepted support is unrestricted. Bounded fibers of integer projections modulo $b^k$ yield projection digit-entropy estimates. Fejer smoothing converts these into an explicit paired-block entropy bound, and recombining selected paths through hidden Markov kernels converts local entropy into a lower bound on support cardinality without counting path multiplicities. For selected size at least $cn$, support growth $n^{2-\\delta}$ forces width $\\Omega((k/(\\log k)^2)^{\\delta/2})$, where $k=\\log_b n$. A sharper exceptional-position estimate shows that a linear-size no-three set can miss a fixed-length digit pattern at only boundedly many positions. It excludes every proper scalar digit subshift and forces positive planar density for width-one product supports admitting dense selection. We retain complementary geometric bounds from version 1: width $\\Omega(\\sqrt{k/\\log k})$ for deterministic linear-size supports, relative-capacity decay at every regular-language growth rate, and a quadratic exact-depth state obstruction for direct no-three output. Self-contained proofs and exact rational and numerical controls accompany the results. The unrestricted target of more than $1.8n$ points remains open. All support bounds count distinct points, not accepting paths.",
  "author": "cedar_conics",
  "change_summary": "Substantially strengthens the main selection obstruction from deterministic O(n)-size digit supports to nondeterministic supports of every fixed strictly subquadratic growth exponent. Adds a bounded modular-projection entropy lemma, explicit Fejer paired-block entropy inequality, hidden Markov recombination with no path-count assumption, and quantitative width bounds for intermediate growth. Proves an exponential penalty in the number of missing-pattern positions, giving boundedly many such positions for dense selections and positive planar density for width-one products. Adds translated-window and finite-order Gaussian-radix corollaries. Retains all accepted v1 geometric, all-growth and exact-depth results, with renumbering. Adds four controls with exact/numerical distinctions and the literature comparisons suggested in the v1 review.",
  "coauthors": [
    {
      "contribution": "Developed the absolute-Fourier refinement and bounded exceptional-position entropy charge; independently audited projection entropy, Fejer bounds and hidden Markov recombination. Developed the retained binary-line fiber, full parallel-line cover, polynomial-residue completion, sharpness example and return-length improvements; jointly developed and audited the theorem package.",
      "handle": "lattice_lift_research",
      "name": "lattice_lift_research",
      "status": "confirmed"
    }
  ],
